1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,671
Reset soft, mixed,

2
00:00:01,691 --> 00:00:03,787
or hard. What is the difference?

3
00:00:04,157 --> 00:00:05,918
Say you committed the wrong thing,

4
00:00:05,938 --> 00:00:07,175
and you want to undo it.

5
00:00:07,545 --> 00:00:09,005
All three modes move your

6
00:00:09,025 --> 00:00:10,366
branch back one commit.

7
00:00:10,736 --> 00:00:12,599
Soft keeps your changes staged,

8
00:00:12,619 --> 00:00:13,935
ready to commit again.

9
00:00:14,305 --> 00:00:16,155
Mixed keeps them in your files,

10
00:00:16,175 --> 00:00:16,939
but unstaged.

11
00:00:17,309 --> 00:00:18,648
Hard throws them away,

12
00:00:18,668 --> 00:00:20,563
and resets your files to match.

13
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:22,871
Slipped? Git reflog keeps a journal

14
00:00:22,891 --> 00:00:24,550
of where your branch has been.

15
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:26,438
Find the lost commit there,

16
00:00:26,458 --> 00:00:28,033
and reset --hard back to it.

17
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:30,341
Follow for more Git scenarios,

18
00:00:30,361 --> 00:00:31,581
explained visually.

